WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.510
No product code existed before the event.

2
00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.816
We built Muse Recall this week.

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.919
I save one project decision.

4
00:00:07.358 --> 00:00:10.188
Here it is a visual direction, but it could be

5
00:00:10.218 --> 00:00:15.210
any rule: a library, an API contract, an
accessibility requirement.

6
00:00:15.828 --> 00:00:19.268
Then I ask Muse Spark for a farm-animal memory
game;

7
00:00:19.612 --> 00:00:21.172
generation is sped up.

8
00:00:21.466 --> 00:00:24.806
The page follows the decision, and I approve
version one.

9
00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:27.339
A fresh page, no request history.

10
00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:29.712
I ask for a Next Level button.

11
00:00:30.073 --> 00:00:33.513
Guard says not verified, so I reject the change.

12
00:00:33.978 --> 00:00:36.558
The decision changed, so I correct the memory.

13
00:00:36.921 --> 00:00:40.841
The old record becomes superseded, the new
decision becomes active,

14
00:00:41.361 --> 00:00:42.941
and the reason stays in history.

15
00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.494
Same request again, and the old decision comes
back.

16
00:00:46.923 --> 00:00:48.003
Guard flags it.

17
00:00:48.212 --> 00:00:51.672
It is advisory and never blocks, so I reject it.

18
00:00:51.943 --> 00:00:54.653
Now I ask for the button, and tell Muse Spark

19
00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:57.503
to follow the project's current decisions from
memory.

20
00:00:57.987 --> 00:01:01.337
The source follows the corrected decision, and
Guard reports no

21
00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:05.047
violation by its supported checks, which is not
a certificate.

22
00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:08.161
I approve version two, button included.

23
00:01:08.687 --> 00:01:10.107
Here is where Meta is used.

24
00:01:10.698 --> 00:01:13.848
The Muse Code CLI generates and changes
applications.

25
00:01:13.878 --> 00:01:20.320
Meta media APIs handle image generation and
editing, segmentation, transcription,

26
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.820
and visual review.

27
00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.432
Each decision keeps its source and history.

28
00:01:24.462 --> 00:01:27.007
Inspect what a generation received,

29
00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:31.267
then export and import memory with its
replacement links intact.

30
00:01:31.772 --> 00:01:34.912
The project keeps its reasons as the application
changes.

31
00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:38.087
The beta brings references into that same
workflow.

32
00:01:38.576 --> 00:01:41.976
Upload an image, generate one, or edit an asset.

33
00:01:42.486 --> 00:01:45.506
Meta's SAM isolates an object from a reference
image.

34
00:01:45.924 --> 00:01:49.594
We review the transparent cutout, approve it,
and insert it

35
00:01:49.624 --> 00:01:51.044
into an application request.

36
00:01:51.498 --> 00:01:55.497
These are retained real model results; the
approval and insertion

37
00:01:55.527 --> 00:01:56.947
are replayed here.

38
00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.865
Voice and video can be project sources too:
record or

39
00:02:00.895 --> 00:02:05.295
upload, play back, transcribe speech, and
inspect a clip.

40
00:02:05.576 --> 00:02:07.676
Suggested decisions wait for confirmation.

41
00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:11.649
These features help assemble the brief; they do
not approve

42
00:02:11.679 --> 00:02:12.109
the work.

43
00:02:12.139 --> 00:02:16.224
Capture the preview and review that frame
against selected decision

44
00:02:16.254 --> 00:02:16.774
revisions.

45
00:02:17.379 --> 00:02:20.359
Screenshot review offers findings and
uncertainty.

46
00:02:20.936 --> 00:02:24.156
It changes no application and approves nothing.

47
00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.680
Source-based Decision Guard is separate.

48
00:02:27.375 --> 00:02:29.985
Both are advisory, and neither certifies
correctness.

49
00:02:30.015 --> 00:02:32.607
Does remembered context help?

50
00:02:32.936 --> 00:02:37.966
In Phase seventeen, original-rule violations
fell from thirty-seven of fifty-seven

51
00:02:37.996 --> 00:02:42.366
to zero of fifty-eight on Muse Spark, and forty-
nine of

52
00:02:42.396 --> 00:02:45.516
sixty to one of sixty on Muse Spark Open.

53
00:02:45.808 --> 00:02:50.268
Four hundred eighty runs, six fixed tasks,
source-code checks.

54
00:02:50.628 --> 00:02:54.498
That trial does not establish general
correctness or validate the

55
00:02:54.528 --> 00:02:55.358
newer media features.

56
00:02:55.388 --> 00:02:57.022
Muse Recall.

57
00:02:57.574 --> 00:02:59.194
The memory your project keeps.
